`files/testcase.py` shows each test creates a new `Faker()` and calls `fake.binary(length)` without any seeding. In `faker/generator.py`, `_is_seeded` starts as `False` and only becomes `True` if `seed()` or `seed_instance()` is called. So in `faker/providers/misc/__init__.py`, `Provider.binary` takes the unseeded branch and returns `os.urandom(length)`. That means the result is sourced from OS entropy rather than the deterministic seeded PRNG path, so it is not identical across independent runs for all lengths; only `length == 0` is always `b''`. Therefore the invariant does not hold across all 15 parametrized cases.

